README.md:3:Neon Pairs is a memory game that runs offline from one HTML file and keeps local best moves for each board size.
README.md:30:Open Reproduce a game to load a board code or export progress. Loading an unfinished snapshot pauses it. Resume returns focus to the remembered card and continues the remaining mismatch interval. A completed snapshot loads as completed without Resume. Elapsed time stops at 359999999ms while play continues. The minutes and seconds display reaches 5999:59. Moves stop at 999999. Matching and victory continue at that count. Saved bests use the same move limit.
docs/controls.md:51:- C12 - A loaded completed snapshot keeps the win banner static and plays no celebration. Import doesn't write a best score. Resuming an unfinished snapshot and later winning records a local best under R10.
docs/controls.md:53:For example, loading a completed game with fewer moves than the saved best shows that game without replacing the saved record.
